<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.15.6: Lesson Summary</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01141</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.15.6: Lesson Summary</md:title>
    <md:uuid>1bb204ee-b903-45fe-ab03-8e1ecacf5ba4</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you learned how to:</para>
<list>
  <item>
    Find missing terms in a geometric sequence.
  </item>
</list>
<para>Here are the <emphasis>activities </emphasis>that helped you reach those goals:</para>
<list>
  <item>
    4.15.1: What Are the Patterns?
  </item>
  <list>
    <item>
      In this activity, you noticed and wondered about the patterns and characteristics of different sequences. 
    </item>
  </list>
  <item>
    4.15.2: Using Tables and Graphs to Represent Geometric Sequences
  </item>
  <list>
    <item>
      In this activity, you used tables and graphs to recognize a sequence and find the next term. You learned that geometric sequences can get larger or smaller.
    </item>
    <item>
      4.15.2: Self Check 
    </item>
    <item>
      4.15.2: Additional Resources 
    </item>
  </list>
  <item>
    4.15.3: Complete the Sequence
  </item>
  <list>
    <item>
      In this activity, you worked to complete the geometric sequences by filling in the blanks. You used a common ratio to find the pattern to complete the sequence.
    </item>
    <item>
      4.15.3: Self Check 
    </item>
    <item>
      4.15.3: Additional Resources 
    </item>
  </list>
  <item>
    4.15.4: Connecting the Common Ratio and the Term in a Sequence
  </item>
  <list>
    <item>
      In this activity, you summarized what you learned in the lesson by explaining why a sequence is geometric and how you are able to find the next term.
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para>After these activities, you completed the following <emphasis>practice</emphasis>:</para>
<list>
  <item>
    4.15.5: Practice
  </item>
</list>
<title>Checking In</title>
